WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
Say an airline wants a
fleet of new passenger jets.

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.720
Who can it call?

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.610
Basically two companies.

4
00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:09.670
They make most of the
world's large passenger jets.

5
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:14.920
In 2023, Boeing delivered
528 commercial aircraft,

6
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.160
and Airbus delivered 735.

7
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.340
Hair salons, meanwhile,
number in the thousands.

8
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.440
So why do some industries
have thousands of small firms,

9
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.850
while others have only two or three?

10
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.850
In this mission, you'll build
the long-run average total

11
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.370
cost curve from short-run curves.

12
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:37.780
Then you'll map where economies of scale
end and diseconomies of scale begin.

13
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.650
Your mission: explain why some
industries hold many firms

14
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.150
and others just a few.
